## Testing conventions

- **Red → green → refactor.** A failing test comes first; a change without a test is incomplete.
- **One behaviour per test**, named for the requirement it proves. Tag the requirement id in the
  test name or the nearest comment when a requirement exists.
- **Test pyramid**: many fast unit tests, few integration tests, end-to-end only for the critical
  paths.
- **Determinism**: no sleeps, no real network, no wall-clock or timezone dependence. Freeze time
  explicitly when time matters.
- **Coverage is a signal, not a goal**: cover the branches that carry risk, not every line.
- For advanced techniques (fixtures, property-based, contract, mutation) load the FlowForge
  `forge-dev-testing` skill before designing the suite.
